LUAI_EXTRASPACE = sizeof(RobloxExtraSpace) (44 bytes) and the luai_userstate* hooks construct,
destroy and reset it (2016 shape, 2013 layout; stand-in class, see the comment in the patch).

Justification (PLAYER bytes): luaE_newthread 0x00876420 allocates 0xa4 = 0x78 + 0x2c and returns
block+0x2c; lua_newstate 0x00876a00 allocates 0x1a4 and places the root extra space with an
out-of-line RobloxExtraSpace() 0x00876970 under an EH state (placement new); lua_newthread
0x008750b0 calls RobloxExtraSpace::constructChild(L1, L-0x2c) 0x00875050 (iOS 10-29 transfer
mislabels that one "lua_newthread"), which calls RobloxExtraSpace(RobloxExtraSpace*) 0x00874f40;
luaE_freethread 0x00876830 and lua_close 0x008768a0 call ~RobloxExtraSpace 0x008766a0 on L-0x2c;
lua_resume 0x008ab8e0 clears bit 0 of byte [L-0x10] (yieldCaptured, a 1-bit unit of its own at
+0x1c; identity:5 is the low 5 bits of the dword at +0x18 per 0x00874f40, so 2013 used two
allocation units where 2016 packs one, 44 vs 40 bytes). The ctor at 0x00874f40 asserts at
luaconf.h:852 (push 0x354); the bodies are RBX code and are not reproduced here.

--- a/luaconf.h
+++ b/luaconf.h
@@ -720,7 +720,55 @@
